{
    "post_id": 68253,
    "title": "שֶֽׂרַח בַּת־אָשֵׁר | Seraḥ bat Asher — a havdalah piyyuṭ by Isaac Gantwerk Mayer",
    "author": "Isaac Gantwerk Mayer",
    "coauthors": [
        {
            "name": "Isaac Gantwerk Mayer",
            "bio": "From a family of musicians, Isaac Gantwerk Mayer believes that creative art is one of the most powerful ways to get in touch with the divine. He composes music and poetry in Hebrew and English. (He also <a href=\"/index.php?user_ID=342\">translates</a> and <a href=\"/index.php?user_ID=820\">transcribes</a> Hebrew and Aramaic texts, adding <em>niqqud</em> and <em>t'amim</em> as needed.) Isaac runs a Jewish music transcription service, which will transcribe and set any Jewish music in any language, recorded or written. Contact his service on <a href=\"https://www.facebook.com/pg/isaacgmayerjewishtranscription/\">Facebook</a> or via <a href=\"https://igmjewishcreativeworks.com/contact\">his music blog</a>.",
            "website": "https://igmjewishcreativeworks.com",
            "avatar": "https://opensiddur.org/wp-content/uploads/2021/12/isaac-gantwerk-mayer-2021-e1674561264977-96x96.jpg",
            "profile_link": "https://opensiddur.org/profile/isaac-gantwerk-mayer"
        }
    ],
    "date": "2026-07-12",
    "last_updated": "2026-07-29",
    "excerpt": "In the style of the full Eliyahu haNavi piyyuṭ recited by some communities every Havdalah, a piyyuṭ in honor of Seraḥ bat Asher, retelling the events of her life according to the midrashim. This is not the first time I've written a Havdalah piece on Seraḥ, the distaff counterpart to Elijah in the midrash. She also inspired <a href=\"/?p=37932\">this shorter song</a>. Like the full Eliyahu haNavi piyyuṭ, this is in three-line rhyming stanzas with a repeated refrain. Unlike it, it is in a tashraq reverse alphabetical acrostic, followed by an authorial tag — this time using a matronymic.",
    "content": "<div class=\"english\" lang=\"eng-Latn\" style=\"font-size: 1.2em;\">\nIn the style of the full Eliyahu haNavi piyyuṭ recited by some communities every Havdalah, a piyyuṭ in honor of Seraḥ bat Asher, retelling the events of her life according to the midrashim. This is not the first time I&#8217;ve written a Havdalah piece on Seraḥ, the distaff counterpart to Elijah in the midrash. She also inspired <a href=\"/?p=37932\">this shorter song</a>. Like the full Eliyahu haNavi piyyuṭ, this is in three-line rhyming stanzas with a repeated refrain. Unlike it, it is in a tashraq reverse alphabetical acrostic, followed by an authorial tag — this time using a matronymic.\n</div>\n<hr />\n<table style=\"margin-left: auto; margin-right: auto;\" class=\"draggable toggleable-table\">\n<thead>\n<tr>\n<th id=\"x\" style=\"text-align: right;\">Source (Hebrew)</th>\n<th style=\"text-align: left;\">Translation (English)</th>\n</tr>\n</thead>\n<tbody>\n<tr>\n<td style=\"vertical-align:top;\">\n<div class=\"liturgy\" lang=\"heb-Hebr\" style=\"text-align: right;\">\nשֶֽׂרַח בַּת־אָשֵׁר, שֶֽׂרַח בַּת־אָשֵׁר, שֶֽׂרַח בַּת־אָשֵׁר<br />\nבִּמְהֵרָה בֵּין אָב לְבֵן, בֵּין אֵם לְבַת הִיא תְּפַשֵּׁר׃\n</div>\n</td>\n<td style=\"vertical-align:top;\">\n<div class=\"english\" lang=\"eng-Latn\" style=\"text-align: left;\">\nSeraḥ daughter of Asher, <span class=\"instruction\">(×3)</span><br />\nspeedily, between father and son, between mother and daughter she will reconcile.\n</div>\n</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td style=\"vertical-align:top;\">\n<div class=\"liturgy\" lang=\"heb-Hebr\" style=\"text-align: right;\">\n<span class=\"acrostic\">תּ</span>וֹרָה הַקְּדוֹשָׁה מַזְכִּירָתָהּ פַּעֲמַֽיִם<br />\n<span class=\"acrostic\">שְׁ</span>מָהּ נִמְצֵאת בְּסֵֽפֶר בְּרִיאַת אֶֽרֶץ וְשָׁמַֽיִם<br />\n<span class=\"acrostic\">רְ</span>שׁוּמָה בְּמִפְקַד פִּינְחָס כִּי הָלְכָה בְּתוֹךְ הַמַּיִם׃<br />\nשֶֽׂרַח בַּת־אָשֵׁר…\n</div>\n</td>\n<td style=\"vertical-align:top;\">\n<div class=\"english\" lang=\"eng-Latn\" style=\"text-align: left;\">\nThe holy Torah mentions her twice!<span class=\"footnote_referrer\"><a role=\"button\" tabindex=\"0\" onclick=\"footnote_moveToReference__1('footnote_plugin_reference__1_1');\" onkeypress=\"footnote_moveToReference__1('footnote_plugin_reference__1_1');\" ><sup id=\"footnote_plugin_tooltip__1_1\" class=\"footnote_plugin_tooltip_text\">[1]</sup></a><span id=\"footnote_plugin_tooltip_text__1_1\" class=\"footnote_tooltip\"> Seraḥ is mentioned in Genesis 46:17 (Genesis being the book of creation) and Numbers 26:46 (in the census in the portion of Pinḥas). From this the rabbis determine that she lived through the exile of Egypt.&nbsp;</span></span><script type=\"text/javascript\"> jQuery('#footnote_plugin_tooltip__1_1').tooltip({ tip: '#footnote_plugin_tooltip_text__1_1', tipClass: 'footnote_tooltip', effect: 'fade', predelay: 0, fadeInSpeed: 200, delay: 400, fadeOutSpeed: 200, position: 'center right', relative: true, offset: [0, 0], });</script> <span class=\"acrostic\">&nbsp;</span><br />\nHer name is found in the book of creation of earth and heaven; <span class=\"acrostic\">&nbsp;</span><br />\nlisted in Pinḥas’ census for she went in the midst of the water. <span class=\"acrostic\">&nbsp;</span><br />\nSeraḥ daughter of Asher…\n</div>\n</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td style=\"vertical-align:top;\">\n<div class=\"liturgy\" lang=\"heb-Hebr\" style=\"text-align: right;\">\n<span class=\"acrostic\">קָ</span>מָה מִבֶּֽטֶן אֵֽשֶׁת אָבִֽיהָ בָּרוּךְ מִבָּנִים<br />\n<span class=\"acrostic\">צִ</span>דְקָנִית הָיְתָה וְנוֹדְעוּ־לָהּ כׇּל־טְמוּנִים<br />\n<span class=\"acrostic\">פֵּ</span>רוּשׁ הַחֲכָמִים חַיֶּֽיהָ אֲרֻכֵּי שָׁנִים׃<br />\nשֶֽׂרַח בַּת־אָשֵׁר…\n</div>\n</td>\n<td style=\"vertical-align:top;\">\n<div class=\"english\" lang=\"eng-Latn\" style=\"text-align: left;\">\nShe came from the womb of the wife<span class=\"footnote_referrer\"><a role=\"button\" tabindex=\"0\" onclick=\"footnote_moveToReference__1('footnote_plugin_reference__1_2');\" onkeypress=\"footnote_moveToReference__1('footnote_plugin_reference__1_2');\" ><sup id=\"footnote_plugin_tooltip__1_2\" class=\"footnote_plugin_tooltip_text\">[2]</sup></a><span id=\"footnote_plugin_tooltip_text__1_2\" class=\"footnote_tooltip\"> According to some midrashim (for instance, Sefer haYashar, Vayeshev 21; see also Ḥizkuni on Numbers 26:46, who cites a variant text of Targum Onkelos that we no longer have), Seraḥ was not directly the daughter of Asher, but rather the daughter of Asher’s wife who was adopted by him when she married into the family.&nbsp;</span></span><script type=\"text/javascript\"> jQuery('#footnote_plugin_tooltip__1_2').tooltip({ tip: '#footnote_plugin_tooltip_text__1_2', tipClass: 'footnote_tooltip', effect: 'fade', predelay: 0, fadeInSpeed: 200, delay: 400, fadeOutSpeed: 200, position: 'center right', relative: true, offset: [0, 0], });</script> of her father, most blessed of sons.<span class=\"footnote_referrer\"><a role=\"button\" tabindex=\"0\" onclick=\"footnote_moveToReference__1('footnote_plugin_reference__1_3');\" onkeypress=\"footnote_moveToReference__1('footnote_plugin_reference__1_3');\" ><sup id=\"footnote_plugin_tooltip__1_3\" class=\"footnote_plugin_tooltip_text\">[3]</sup></a><span id=\"footnote_plugin_tooltip_text__1_3\" class=\"footnote_tooltip\"> Asher — see Deuteronomy 33:24&nbsp;</span></span><script type=\"text/javascript\"> jQuery('#footnote_plugin_tooltip__1_3').tooltip({ tip: '#footnote_plugin_tooltip_text__1_3', tipClass: 'footnote_tooltip', effect: 'fade', predelay: 0, fadeInSpeed: 200, delay: 400, fadeOutSpeed: 200, position: 'center right', relative: true, offset: [0, 0], });</script> <span class=\"acrostic\">&nbsp;</span><br />\nShe was righteous and all hidden things were revealed to her. <span class=\"acrostic\">&nbsp;</span><br />\nThe sages interpreted that her life was long of years. <span class=\"acrostic\">&nbsp;</span><br />\nSeraḥ daughter of Asher…\n</div>\n</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td style=\"vertical-align:top;\">\n<div class=\"liturgy\" lang=\"heb-Hebr\" style=\"text-align: right;\">\n<span class=\"acrostic\">עָ</span>נְתָה לַתָּם בִּלְשׁוֹן תֵּמַהּ כִּי יוֹסֵף בְּמִצְרַֽיִם<br />\n<span class=\"acrostic\">שָׂ</span>מַח בָּהּ כִּי אָמְרָה לֵאמֹר יוּלְדוּ לוֹ עַל־בִּרְכַּֽיִם<br />\n<span class=\"acrostic\">נִ</span>ינֶֽיךָ מְבֹרְכֵי־הָאֵל מְנַשֶּׁה וְאֶפְרַֽיִם׃<br />\nשֶֽׂרַח בַּת־אָשֵׁר…\n</div>\n</td>\n<td style=\"vertical-align:top;\">\n<div class=\"english\" lang=\"eng-Latn\" style=\"text-align: left;\">\nShe answered the pure one<span class=\"footnote_referrer\"><a role=\"button\" tabindex=\"0\" onclick=\"footnote_moveToReference__1('footnote_plugin_reference__1_4');\" onkeypress=\"footnote_moveToReference__1('footnote_plugin_reference__1_4');\" ><sup id=\"footnote_plugin_tooltip__1_4\" class=\"footnote_plugin_tooltip_text\">[4]</sup></a><span id=\"footnote_plugin_tooltip_text__1_4\" class=\"footnote_tooltip\"> Jacob&nbsp;</span></span><script type=\"text/javascript\"> jQuery('#footnote_plugin_tooltip__1_4').tooltip({ tip: '#footnote_plugin_tooltip_text__1_4', tipClass: 'footnote_tooltip', effect: 'fade', predelay: 0, fadeInSpeed: 200, delay: 400, fadeOutSpeed: 200, position: 'center right', relative: true, offset: [0, 0], });</script> in wondrous tone that Joseph was in Egypt.<span class=\"footnote_referrer\"><a role=\"button\" tabindex=\"0\" onclick=\"footnote_moveToReference__1('footnote_plugin_reference__1_5');\" onkeypress=\"footnote_moveToReference__1('footnote_plugin_reference__1_5');\" ><sup id=\"footnote_plugin_tooltip__1_5\" class=\"footnote_plugin_tooltip_text\">[5]</sup></a><span id=\"footnote_plugin_tooltip_text__1_5\" class=\"footnote_tooltip\"> One of the oldest legends about Seraḥ, found already in the Targum Pseudo-Jonathan for Numbers 26:46. This stanza’s retelling is based on  that of the Midrash HaGadol on Genesis 45:26, discussed by Prof. RabbiRachel Adelman in &#8220;<a href=\"https://www.thetorah.com/article/serach-jacobs-immortal-granddaughter\">Serach, Jacob’s Immortal Granddaughter</a>&#8221; (at thetorah.com, 18 January 2024).&nbsp;</span></span><script type=\"text/javascript\"> jQuery('#footnote_plugin_tooltip__1_5').tooltip({ tip: '#footnote_plugin_tooltip_text__1_5', tipClass: 'footnote_tooltip', effect: 'fade', predelay: 0, fadeInSpeed: 200, delay: 400, fadeOutSpeed: 200, position: 'center right', relative: true, offset: [0, 0], });</script> <span class=\"acrostic\">&nbsp;</span><br />\nHe rejoiced in her for she told him, “born to him on the knees <span class=\"acrostic\">&nbsp;</span><br />\nare your grandchildren, blessed of <span class=\"divine-referent\">the Deity</span>, Manasseh and Ephraim! <span class=\"acrostic\">&nbsp;</span><br />\nSeraḥ daughter of Asher…\n</div>\n</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td style=\"vertical-align:top;\">\n<div class=\"liturgy\" lang=\"heb-Hebr\" style=\"text-align: right;\">\n<span class=\"acrostic\">מ</span>וֹרִיד שְׁאוֹל וַיָּֽעַל הוֹרִידָהּ לְאַדְמַת חַם<br />\n<span class=\"acrostic\">לִ</span>רְאוֹת אֵיפֹה בַּיְאֹר קֶֽבֶר הַצַּדִּיק תֻּחַם<br />\n<span class=\"acrostic\">כִּ</span>לּוּ שְׁנוֹת שִׁעְבּוּד בָּא עֵת הָעָם שֶׁיְּנֻחַם׃<br />\nשֶֽׂרַח בַּת־אָשֵׁר…\n</div>\n</td>\n<td style=\"vertical-align:top;\">\n<div class=\"english\" lang=\"eng-Latn\" style=\"text-align: left;\">\n<span class=\"divine-referent\">The Bringer-Down-and-Up</span><span class=\"footnote_referrer\"><a role=\"button\" tabindex=\"0\" onclick=\"footnote_moveToReference__1('footnote_plugin_reference__1_6');\" onkeypress=\"footnote_moveToReference__1('footnote_plugin_reference__1_6');\" ><sup id=\"footnote_plugin_tooltip__1_6\" class=\"footnote_plugin_tooltip_text\">[6]</sup></a><span id=\"footnote_plugin_tooltip_text__1_6\" class=\"footnote_tooltip\"> God, according to another well-known Biblical woman, Ḥannah, in I Samuel 2:6&nbsp;</span></span><script type=\"text/javascript\"> jQuery('#footnote_plugin_tooltip__1_6').tooltip({ tip: '#footnote_plugin_tooltip_text__1_6', tipClass: 'footnote_tooltip', effect: 'fade', predelay: 0, fadeInSpeed: 200, delay: 400, fadeOutSpeed: 200, position: 'center right', relative: true, offset: [0, 0], });</script> brought her down to the land of Ḥam,<span class=\"footnote_referrer\"><a role=\"button\" tabindex=\"0\" onclick=\"footnote_moveToReference__1('footnote_plugin_reference__1_7');\" onkeypress=\"footnote_moveToReference__1('footnote_plugin_reference__1_7');\" ><sup id=\"footnote_plugin_tooltip__1_7\" class=\"footnote_plugin_tooltip_text\">[7]</sup></a><span id=\"footnote_plugin_tooltip_text__1_7\" class=\"footnote_tooltip\"> That is, Egypt&nbsp;</span></span><script type=\"text/javascript\"> jQuery('#footnote_plugin_tooltip__1_7').tooltip({ tip: '#footnote_plugin_tooltip_text__1_7', tipClass: 'footnote_tooltip', effect: 'fade', predelay: 0, fadeInSpeed: 200, delay: 400, fadeOutSpeed: 200, position: 'center right', relative: true, offset: [0, 0], });</script> <span class=\"acrostic\">&nbsp;</span><br />\nto see where in the Nile the righteous one’s grave was delineated. <span class=\"acrostic\">&nbsp;</span><br />\nThe years of enslavement ended, the time came for the people to be comforted. <span class=\"acrostic\">&nbsp;</span><br />\nSeraḥ daughter of Asher…\n</div>\n</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td style=\"vertical-align:top;\">\n<div class=\"liturgy\" lang=\"heb-Hebr\" style=\"text-align: right;\">\n<span class=\"acrostic\">יָ</span>שָׁר לַאֲתַר הִדְרִיכַֽתּוּ הׇעֳלָה מֵהַסּוּף<br />\n<span class=\"acrostic\">טֻ</span>בְּעוּ צִבְאוֹת פַּרְעֹה וְהִיא עָבְרָה מִתּוֹךְ יַם סוּף<br />\n<span class=\"acrostic\">חָ</span>זְתָה בְּאֶמְפּוֹמָטָא כְּזֹֽהַר הַפַּרְצוּף׃<br />\nשֶֽׂרַח בַּת־אָשֵׁר…\n</div>\n</td>\n<td style=\"vertical-align:top;\">\n<div class=\"english\" lang=\"eng-Latn\" style=\"text-align: left;\">\nRight to the site she led him; it was raised from the reeds.<span class=\"footnote_referrer\"><a role=\"button\" tabindex=\"0\" onclick=\"footnote_moveToReference__1('footnote_plugin_reference__1_8');\" onkeypress=\"footnote_moveToReference__1('footnote_plugin_reference__1_8');\" ><sup id=\"footnote_plugin_tooltip__1_8\" class=\"footnote_plugin_tooltip_text\">[8]</sup></a><span id=\"footnote_plugin_tooltip_text__1_8\" class=\"footnote_tooltip\"> Joseph’s coffin, according to sources such as the Talmud Bavli, Sotah 13a, was sunk into the Nile by the Egyptians. Seraḥ pointed this out to Moshe so that the Israelites could retrieve it and fulfill Josephs’ final request that his body be taken home.&nbsp;</span></span><script type=\"text/javascript\"> jQuery('#footnote_plugin_tooltip__1_8').tooltip({ tip: '#footnote_plugin_tooltip_text__1_8', tipClass: 'footnote_tooltip', effect: 'fade', predelay: 0, fadeInSpeed: 200, delay: 400, fadeOutSpeed: 200, position: 'center right', relative: true, offset: [0, 0], });</script> <span class=\"acrostic\">&nbsp;</span><br />\nThe armies of Pharaoh sunk and she passed through the Reed Sea. <span class=\"acrostic\">&nbsp;</span><br />\nShe saw the stained-glass<span class=\"footnote_referrer\"><a role=\"button\" tabindex=\"0\" onclick=\"footnote_moveToReference__1('footnote_plugin_reference__1_9');\" onkeypress=\"footnote_moveToReference__1('footnote_plugin_reference__1_9');\" ><sup id=\"footnote_plugin_tooltip__1_9\" class=\"footnote_plugin_tooltip_text\">[9]</sup></a><span id=\"footnote_plugin_tooltip_text__1_9\" class=\"footnote_tooltip\"> Pesikta d-Rav Kahana 11:13&nbsp;</span></span><script type=\"text/javascript\"> jQuery('#footnote_plugin_tooltip__1_9').tooltip({ tip: '#footnote_plugin_tooltip_text__1_9', tipClass: 'footnote_tooltip', effect: 'fade', predelay: 0, fadeInSpeed: 200, delay: 400, fadeOutSpeed: 200, position: 'center right', relative: true, offset: [0, 0], });</script> like the radiance of the Countenance. <span class=\"acrostic\">&nbsp;</span><br />\nSeraḥ daughter of Asher…\n</div>\n</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td style=\"vertical-align:top;\">\n<div class=\"liturgy\" lang=\"heb-Hebr\" style=\"text-align: right;\">\n<span class=\"acrostic\">זָ</span>כְתָה לַעֲלוֹת לָאָֽרֶץ שֶׁמִּשָּׁם יָרְדָה לְפָנִים<br />\n<span class=\"acrostic\">וְ</span>שָׁם אָבֵֽלָה בֵּית הַמַּעֲכָה פָּנְתָה פָנִים<br />\n<span class=\"acrostic\">הָ</span>יְתָה חֲכָמָה בְּעִירָהּ מִכׇּל־הַמְּבִינִים׃<br />\nשֶֽׂרַח בַּת־אָשֵׁר…\n</div>\n</td>\n<td style=\"vertical-align:top;\">\n<div class=\"english\" lang=\"eng-Latn\" style=\"text-align: left;\">\nShe merited to go up to the land from where she had previously descended, <span class=\"acrostic\">&nbsp;</span><br />\nand there to Abel-Beth-Maacah she turned her face; <span class=\"acrostic\">&nbsp;</span><br />\nshe was wise in her city<span class=\"footnote_referrer\"><a role=\"button\" tabindex=\"0\" onclick=\"footnote_moveToReference__1('footnote_plugin_reference__1_10');\" onkeypress=\"footnote_moveToReference__1('footnote_plugin_reference__1_10');\" ><sup id=\"footnote_plugin_tooltip__1_10\" class=\"footnote_plugin_tooltip_text\">[10]</sup></a><span id=\"footnote_plugin_tooltip_text__1_10\" class=\"footnote_tooltip\"> According to the midrash Bereshit Rabbah 94:9, the wise woman of Abeh-Beth-Maacah mentioned in II Samuel 20 was Seraḥ.&nbsp;</span></span><script type=\"text/javascript\"> jQuery('#footnote_plugin_tooltip__1_10').tooltip({ tip: '#footnote_plugin_tooltip_text__1_10', tipClass: 'footnote_tooltip', effect: 'fade', predelay: 0, fadeInSpeed: 200, delay: 400, fadeOutSpeed: 200, position: 'center right', relative: true, offset: [0, 0], });</script> over all with understanding. <span class=\"acrostic\">&nbsp;</span><br />\nSeraḥ daughter of Asher…\n</div>\n</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td style=\"vertical-align:top;\">\n<div class=\"liturgy\" lang=\"heb-Hebr\" style=\"text-align: right;\">\n<span class=\"acrostic\">דַּ</span>בֵּר יְדַבְּרוּ רִאשֹׁנָה לֵאמֹר שָׁאוֹל וְכֵן<br />\n<span class=\"acrostic\">גַּ</span>ם עֵת צָרָה בָּאָה אֵלֶֽיהָ כִּי הָיָה שׁוֹכֵן<br />\n<span class=\"acrostic\">בֶּ</span>ן־בִּכְרִי שָׂם בָּעִיר וָאֵם אִישׁ צַר וּמְסַכֵּן׃<br />\nשֶֽׂרַח בַּת־אָשֵׁר…\n</div>\n</td>\n<td style=\"vertical-align:top;\">\n<div class=\"english\" lang=\"eng-Latn\" style=\"text-align: left;\">\nThey would speak, speaking back then, saying “Ask[foott]II Samuel 20:18[/foot] etc.” <span class=\"acrostic\">&nbsp;</span><br />\nSo too, a time of stress came to her, for dwelling there in the mother city<span class=\"footnote_referrer\"><a role=\"button\" tabindex=\"0\" onclick=\"footnote_moveToReference__1('footnote_plugin_reference__1_11');\" onkeypress=\"footnote_moveToReference__1('footnote_plugin_reference__1_11');\" ><sup id=\"footnote_plugin_tooltip__1_11\" class=\"footnote_plugin_tooltip_text\">[11]</sup></a><span id=\"footnote_plugin_tooltip_text__1_11\" class=\"footnote_tooltip\"> Literally: “city and mother,” II Samuel 20:19&nbsp;</span></span><script type=\"text/javascript\"> jQuery('#footnote_plugin_tooltip__1_11').tooltip({ tip: '#footnote_plugin_tooltip_text__1_11', tipClass: 'footnote_tooltip', effect: 'fade', predelay: 0, fadeInSpeed: 200, delay: 400, fadeOutSpeed: 200, position: 'center right', relative: true, offset: [0, 0], });</script> <span class=\"acrostic\">&nbsp;</span><br />\nwas the son of Bikhri,<span class=\"footnote_referrer\"><a role=\"button\" tabindex=\"0\" onclick=\"footnote_moveToReference__1('footnote_plugin_reference__1_12');\" onkeypress=\"footnote_moveToReference__1('footnote_plugin_reference__1_12');\" ><sup id=\"footnote_plugin_tooltip__1_12\" class=\"footnote_plugin_tooltip_text\">[12]</sup></a><span id=\"footnote_plugin_tooltip_text__1_12\" class=\"footnote_tooltip\"> Sheba son of Bichri, the rebel against David who fled to Abel-Beth-Maacah and who Joab was ordered to murder.&nbsp;</span></span><script type=\"text/javascript\"> jQuery('#footnote_plugin_tooltip__1_12').tooltip({ tip: '#footnote_plugin_tooltip_text__1_12', tipClass: 'footnote_tooltip', effect: 'fade', predelay: 0, fadeInSpeed: 200, delay: 400, fadeOutSpeed: 200, position: 'center right', relative: true, offset: [0, 0], });</script> an inimical and dangerous man. <span class=\"acrostic\">&nbsp;</span><br />\nSeraḥ daughter of Asher…\n</div>\n</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td style=\"vertical-align:top;\">\n<div class=\"liturgy\" lang=\"heb-Hebr\" style=\"text-align: right;\">\n<span class=\"acrostic\">אֶ</span>ת־יָדוֹ נָשָׂא בַּמֶּֽלֶךְ וְהֵעִיר שָׁם תַּבְהֵלָה<br />\n<span class=\"acrostic\">אָ</span>מַר בֶּן־צְרוּיָה בְּאַפּוֹ לָצוּר בְּסוֹלְלָה<br />\n<span class=\"acrostic\">אָ</span>מְרָה־לוֹ לָֽמָּה תְּמִיתֵֽנוּ אָמַר חָלִֽילָה׃<br />\nשֶֽׂרַח בַּת־אָשֵׁר…\n</div>\n</td>\n<td style=\"vertical-align:top;\">\n<div class=\"english\" lang=\"eng-Latn\" style=\"text-align: left;\">\nHe had raised his hand against the king, and roused panic there. <span class=\"acrostic\">&nbsp;</span><br />\nThe son of Ẓeruyah,<span class=\"footnote_referrer\"><a role=\"button\" tabindex=\"0\" onclick=\"footnote_moveToReference__1('footnote_plugin_reference__1_13');\" onkeypress=\"footnote_moveToReference__1('footnote_plugin_reference__1_13');\" ><sup id=\"footnote_plugin_tooltip__1_13\" class=\"footnote_plugin_tooltip_text\">[13]</sup></a><span id=\"footnote_plugin_tooltip_text__1_13\" class=\"footnote_tooltip\"> Joaḇ. Find II Samuel 20:15&nbsp;</span></span><script type=\"text/javascript\"> jQuery('#footnote_plugin_tooltip__1_13').tooltip({ tip: '#footnote_plugin_tooltip_text__1_13', tipClass: 'footnote_tooltip', effect: 'fade', predelay: 0, fadeInSpeed: 200, delay: 400, fadeOutSpeed: 200, position: 'center right', relative: true, offset: [0, 0], });</script> in his rage, said to besiege with ramparts. <span class=\"acrostic\">&nbsp;</span><br />\nShe said to him, “Why kill us?” He said, “Far be it!”<span class=\"footnote_referrer\"><a role=\"button\" tabindex=\"0\" onclick=\"footnote_moveToReference__1('footnote_plugin_reference__1_14');\" onkeypress=\"footnote_moveToReference__1('footnote_plugin_reference__1_14');\" ><sup id=\"footnote_plugin_tooltip__1_14\" class=\"footnote_plugin_tooltip_text\">[14]</sup></a><span id=\"footnote_plugin_tooltip_text__1_14\" class=\"footnote_tooltip\"> Find II Samuel 20:20–21&nbsp;</span></span><script type=\"text/javascript\"> jQuery('#footnote_plugin_tooltip__1_14').tooltip({ tip: '#footnote_plugin_tooltip_text__1_14', tipClass: 'footnote_tooltip', effect: 'fade', predelay: 0, fadeInSpeed: 200, delay: 400, fadeOutSpeed: 200, position: 'center right', relative: true, offset: [0, 0], });</script> <span class=\"acrostic\">&nbsp;</span><br />\nSeraḥ daughter of Asher…\n</div>\n</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td style=\"vertical-align:top;\">\n<div class=\"liturgy\" lang=\"heb-Hebr\" style=\"text-align: right;\">\n<span class=\"acrostic\">יְ</span>שָׁרָה וַחֲכָמָה אַתְּ חָלִֽילָה אִם־אַשְׁחִית<br />\n<span class=\"acrostic\">צָ</span>עַק יוֹאָב אֵלֶֽיהָ מְבֹרֶֽכֶת וְנִצְחִית<br />\n<span class=\"acrostic\">חִ</span>זְקִי לְהַשְׁלִיךְ רֹאשׁ הַמּוֹרֵד זֽוֹהִי הֶכְרֵחִית׃<br />\nשֶֽׂרַח בַּת־אָשֵׁר…\n</div>\n</td>\n<td style=\"vertical-align:top;\">\n<div class=\"english\" lang=\"eng-Latn\" style=\"text-align: left;\">\nUpright and wise are you; far be it from me to destroy!” <span class=\"acrostic\">&nbsp;</span><br />\ncried Joaḇ to she who is blessed and eternal. <span class=\"acrostic\">&nbsp;</span><br />\n“Strongly throw down the rebel’s head; this is what is necessary!” <span class=\"acrostic\">&nbsp;</span><br />\nSeraḥ daughter of Asher…\n</div>\n</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td style=\"vertical-align:top;\">\n<div class=\"liturgy\" lang=\"heb-Hebr\" style=\"text-align: right;\">\n<span class=\"acrostic\">קָ</span>מָה וְעָשְׂתָה זֹאת הִצִּילָה עִיר בְּחׇכְמָתָהּ<br />\n<span class=\"acrostic\">בִּ</span>זְכוּת כׇּל־חׇכְמוֹת פִּֽיהָ עוֹד דָּבָר שֶׁהִיא זָכְתָה<br />\n<span class=\"acrostic\">נְ</span>וֵה הַגַּן וְהַפַּרְדֵּס בַּחַיִּים רָאֲתָה׃<br />\nשֶֽׂרַח בַּת־אָשֵׁר…\n</div>\n</td>\n<td style=\"vertical-align:top;\">\n<div class=\"english\" lang=\"eng-Latn\" style=\"text-align: left;\">\nShe rose and did this, saving the city in her wisdom. <span class=\"acrostic\">&nbsp;</span><br />\nBy merit of all the wisdom of her mouth, another matter that she merited: <span class=\"acrostic\">&nbsp;</span><br />\nthe abode of the Garden and paradise she saw in her life.<span class=\"footnote_referrer\"><a role=\"button\" tabindex=\"0\" onclick=\"footnote_moveToReference__1('footnote_plugin_reference__1_15');\" onkeypress=\"footnote_moveToReference__1('footnote_plugin_reference__1_15');\" ><sup id=\"footnote_plugin_tooltip__1_15\" class=\"footnote_plugin_tooltip_text\">[15]</sup></a><span id=\"footnote_plugin_tooltip_text__1_15\" class=\"footnote_tooltip\"> Find Derekh Eretz Zuta 1:18, where she is the ninth person listed who entered the Garden of Eden alive.&nbsp;</span></span><script type=\"text/javascript\"> jQuery('#footnote_plugin_tooltip__1_15').tooltip({ tip: '#footnote_plugin_tooltip_text__1_15', tipClass: 'footnote_tooltip', effect: 'fade', predelay: 0, fadeInSpeed: 200, delay: 400, fadeOutSpeed: 200, position: 'center right', relative: true, offset: [0, 0], });</script> <span class=\"acrostic\">&nbsp;</span><br />\nSeraḥ daughter of Asher…\n</div>\n</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td style=\"vertical-align:top;\">\n<div class=\"liturgy\" lang=\"heb-Hebr\" style=\"text-align: right;\">\n<span class=\"acrostic\">יָ</span>שְׁבוּ הָרַבָּנִים בְּבֵית מִדְרָשׁ לָדַֽעַת מָה<br />\n<span class=\"acrostic\">עָ</span>מְדוּ מֵימֵי הַיָּם לִפְנֵי יִשְׂרָאֵל כְּחוֹמָה<br />\n<span class=\"acrostic\">לָ</span>מְדוּ כְּאֶמְפּוֹמָטָא כִּי הִיא הָיְתָה שָֽׁמָּה׃<br />\nשֶֽׂרַח בַּת־אָשֵׁר…\n</div>\n</td>\n<td style=\"vertical-align:top;\">\n<div class=\"english\" lang=\"eng-Latn\" style=\"text-align: left;\">\nThe rabbis sat in the study hall to know how <span class=\"acrostic\">&nbsp;</span><br />\nthe waters of the sea stood before Israel like a wall. <span class=\"acrostic\">&nbsp;</span><br />\nThey learned, “like stained-glass,” for she was there!<span class=\"footnote_referrer\"><a role=\"button\" tabindex=\"0\" onclick=\"footnote_moveToReference__1('footnote_plugin_reference__1_16');\" onkeypress=\"footnote_moveToReference__1('footnote_plugin_reference__1_16');\" ><sup id=\"footnote_plugin_tooltip__1_16\" class=\"footnote_plugin_tooltip_text\">[16]</sup></a><span id=\"footnote_plugin_tooltip_text__1_16\" class=\"footnote_tooltip\"> Pesikta d-Rav Kahana 11:13&nbsp;</span></span><script type=\"text/javascript\"> jQuery('#footnote_plugin_tooltip__1_16').tooltip({ tip: '#footnote_plugin_tooltip_text__1_16', tipClass: 'footnote_tooltip', effect: 'fade', predelay: 0, fadeInSpeed: 200, delay: 400, fadeOutSpeed: 200, position: 'center right', relative: true, offset: [0, 0], });</script> <span class=\"acrostic\">&nbsp;</span><br />\nSeraḥ daughter of Asher…\n</div>\n</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td style=\"vertical-align:top;\">\n<div class=\"liturgy\" lang=\"heb-Hebr\" style=\"text-align: right;\">\n<span class=\"acrostic\">חֲ</span>כָמַת הַחֲכָמוֹת אַתְּ וְתַחְזְרִי בְּשִׁירָה<br />\n<span class=\"acrostic\">זָ</span>קַנְתְּ אַרְבַּֽעַת אֲלָפִים עַל־יַד אֲשֶׁר־בָּרָא<br />\n<span class=\"acrostic\">קֽ</span>וּמִי קַבְּצִי עַמֵּךְ בִּירוּשָׁלַֽיִם הַבִּירָה׃<br />\nשֶֽׂרַח בַּת־אָשֵׁר…\n</div>\n</td>\n<td style=\"vertical-align:top;\">\n<div class=\"english\" lang=\"eng-Latn\" style=\"text-align: left;\">\nThe wisest of wise women are you, and you will return in song; <span class=\"acrostic\">&nbsp;</span><br />\nyou have aged four thousand years by the hand of <span class=\"divine-referent\">the One</span> who created you. <span class=\"acrostic\">&nbsp;</span><br />\nRise, gather your people in Jerusalem the capital! <span class=\"acrostic\">&nbsp;</span><br />\nSeraḥ daughter of Asher…\n</div>\n</td>\n</tr>\n</tbody>\n</table>\n<p>&nbsp;</p>\n<div class=\"speaker-mute footnotes_reference_container\"> <div class=\"footnote_container_prepare\"><p><span role=\"button\" tabindex=\"0\" class=\"footnote_reference_container_label pointer\" onclick=\"footnote_expand_collapse_reference_container__1();\">Notes</span><span role=\"button\" tabindex=\"0\" class=\"footnote_reference_container_collapse_button\" style=\"display: none;; display: none;\" onclick=\"footnote_expand_collapse_reference_container__1();\"></span></p></div> <div id=\"footnote_references_container__1\" style=\"\"><table class=\"footnotes_table footnote-reference-container\"><caption class=\"accessibility\">Notes</caption> <tbody> \r\n\r\n<tr class=\"footnotes_plugin_reference_row\"> <th scope=\"row\" id=\"footnote_plugin_reference__1_1\" class=\"footnote_plugin_index pointer\" onclick=\"footnote_moveToAnchor__1('footnote_plugin_tooltip__1_1');\"><a role=\"button\" tabindex=\"0\" class=\"footnote_plugin_link\" >1</a></th> <td class=\"footnote_plugin_text\">Seraḥ is mentioned in Genesis 46:17 (Genesis being the book of creation) and Numbers 26:46 (in the census in the portion of Pinḥas). From this the rabbis determine that she lived through the exile of Egypt.</td></tr>\r\n\r\n<tr class=\"footnotes_plugin_reference_row\"> <th scope=\"row\" id=\"footnote_plugin_reference__1_2\" class=\"footnote_plugin_index pointer\" onclick=\"footnote_moveToAnchor__1('footnote_plugin_tooltip__1_2');\"><a role=\"button\" tabindex=\"0\" class=\"footnote_plugin_link\" >2</a></th> <td class=\"footnote_plugin_text\">According to some midrashim (for instance, Sefer haYashar, Vayeshev 21; see also Ḥizkuni on Numbers 26:46, who cites a variant text of Targum Onkelos that we no longer have), Seraḥ was not directly the daughter of Asher, but rather the daughter of Asher’s wife who was adopted by him when she married into the family.</td></tr>\r\n\r\n<tr class=\"footnotes_plugin_reference_row\"> <th scope=\"row\" id=\"footnote_plugin_reference__1_3\" class=\"footnote_plugin_index pointer\" onclick=\"footnote_moveToAnchor__1('footnote_plugin_tooltip__1_3');\"><a role=\"button\" tabindex=\"0\" class=\"footnote_plugin_link\" >3</a></th> <td class=\"footnote_plugin_text\">Asher — see Deuteronomy 33:24</td></tr>\r\n\r\n<tr class=\"footnotes_plugin_reference_row\"> <th scope=\"row\" id=\"footnote_plugin_reference__1_4\" class=\"footnote_plugin_index pointer\" onclick=\"footnote_moveToAnchor__1('footnote_plugin_tooltip__1_4');\"><a role=\"button\" tabindex=\"0\" class=\"footnote_plugin_link\" >4</a></th> <td class=\"footnote_plugin_text\">Jacob</td></tr>\r\n\r\n<tr class=\"footnotes_plugin_reference_row\"> <th scope=\"row\" id=\"footnote_plugin_reference__1_5\" class=\"footnote_plugin_index pointer\" onclick=\"footnote_moveToAnchor__1('footnote_plugin_tooltip__1_5');\"><a role=\"button\" tabindex=\"0\" class=\"footnote_plugin_link\" >5</a></th> <td class=\"footnote_plugin_text\">One of the oldest legends about Seraḥ, found already in the Targum Pseudo-Jonathan for Numbers 26:46. This stanza’s retelling is based on  that of the Midrash HaGadol on Genesis 45:26, discussed by Prof. RabbiRachel Adelman in &#8220;<a href=\"https://www.thetorah.com/article/serach-jacobs-immortal-granddaughter\">Serach, Jacob’s Immortal Granddaughter</a>&#8221; (at thetorah.com, 18 January 2024).</td></tr>\r\n\r\n<tr class=\"footnotes_plugin_reference_row\"> <th scope=\"row\" id=\"footnote_plugin_reference__1_6\" class=\"footnote_plugin_index pointer\" onclick=\"footnote_moveToAnchor__1('footnote_plugin_tooltip__1_6');\"><a role=\"button\" tabindex=\"0\" class=\"footnote_plugin_link\" >6</a></th> <td class=\"footnote_plugin_text\">God, according to another well-known Biblical woman, Ḥannah, in I Samuel 2:6</td></tr>\r\n\r\n<tr class=\"footnotes_plugin_reference_row\"> <th scope=\"row\" id=\"footnote_plugin_reference__1_7\" class=\"footnote_plugin_index pointer\" onclick=\"footnote_moveToAnchor__1('footnote_plugin_tooltip__1_7');\"><a role=\"button\" tabindex=\"0\" class=\"footnote_plugin_link\" >7</a></th> <td class=\"footnote_plugin_text\">That is, Egypt</td></tr>\r\n\r\n<tr class=\"footnotes_plugin_reference_row\"> <th scope=\"row\" id=\"footnote_plugin_reference__1_8\" class=\"footnote_plugin_index pointer\" onclick=\"footnote_moveToAnchor__1('footnote_plugin_tooltip__1_8');\"><a role=\"button\" tabindex=\"0\" class=\"footnote_plugin_link\" >8</a></th> <td class=\"footnote_plugin_text\">Joseph’s coffin, according to sources such as the Talmud Bavli, Sotah 13a, was sunk into the Nile by the Egyptians. Seraḥ pointed this out to Moshe so that the Israelites could retrieve it and fulfill Josephs’ final request that his body be taken home.</td></tr>\r\n\r\n<tr class=\"footnotes_plugin_reference_row\"> <th scope=\"row\" id=\"footnote_plugin_reference__1_9\" class=\"footnote_plugin_index pointer\" onclick=\"footnote_moveToAnchor__1('footnote_plugin_tooltip__1_9');\"><a role=\"button\" tabindex=\"0\" class=\"footnote_plugin_link\" >9</a></th> <td class=\"footnote_plugin_text\">Pesikta d-Rav Kahana 11:13</td></tr>\r\n\r\n<tr class=\"footnotes_plugin_reference_row\"> <th scope=\"row\" id=\"footnote_plugin_reference__1_10\" class=\"footnote_plugin_index pointer\" onclick=\"footnote_moveToAnchor__1('footnote_plugin_tooltip__1_10');\"><a role=\"button\" tabindex=\"0\" class=\"footnote_plugin_link\" >10</a></th> <td class=\"footnote_plugin_text\">According to the midrash Bereshit Rabbah 94:9, the wise woman of Abeh-Beth-Maacah mentioned in II Samuel 20 was Seraḥ.</td></tr>\r\n\r\n<tr class=\"footnotes_plugin_reference_row\"> <th scope=\"row\" id=\"footnote_plugin_reference__1_11\" class=\"footnote_plugin_index pointer\" onclick=\"footnote_moveToAnchor__1('footnote_plugin_tooltip__1_11');\"><a role=\"button\" tabindex=\"0\" class=\"footnote_plugin_link\" >11</a></th> <td class=\"footnote_plugin_text\">Literally: “city and mother,” II Samuel 20:19</td></tr>\r\n\r\n<tr class=\"footnotes_plugin_reference_row\"> <th scope=\"row\" id=\"footnote_plugin_reference__1_12\" class=\"footnote_plugin_index pointer\" onclick=\"footnote_moveToAnchor__1('footnote_plugin_tooltip__1_12');\"><a role=\"button\" tabindex=\"0\" class=\"footnote_plugin_link\" >12</a></th> <td class=\"footnote_plugin_text\">Sheba son of Bichri, the rebel against David who fled to Abel-Beth-Maacah and who Joab was ordered to murder.</td></tr>\r\n\r\n<tr class=\"footnotes_plugin_reference_row\"> <th scope=\"row\" id=\"footnote_plugin_reference__1_13\" class=\"footnote_plugin_index pointer\" onclick=\"footnote_moveToAnchor__1('footnote_plugin_tooltip__1_13');\"><a role=\"button\" tabindex=\"0\" class=\"footnote_plugin_link\" >13</a></th> <td class=\"footnote_plugin_text\">Joaḇ. Find II Samuel 20:15</td></tr>\r\n\r\n<tr class=\"footnotes_plugin_reference_row\"> <th scope=\"row\" id=\"footnote_plugin_reference__1_14\" class=\"footnote_plugin_index pointer\" onclick=\"footnote_moveToAnchor__1('footnote_plugin_tooltip__1_14');\"><a role=\"button\" tabindex=\"0\" class=\"footnote_plugin_link\" >14</a></th> <td class=\"footnote_plugin_text\">Find II Samuel 20:20–21</td></tr>\r\n\r\n<tr class=\"footnotes_plugin_reference_row\"> <th scope=\"row\" id=\"footnote_plugin_reference__1_15\" class=\"footnote_plugin_index pointer\" onclick=\"footnote_moveToAnchor__1('footnote_plugin_tooltip__1_15');\"><a role=\"button\" tabindex=\"0\" class=\"footnote_plugin_link\" >15</a></th> <td class=\"footnote_plugin_text\">Find Derekh Eretz Zuta 1:18, where she is the ninth person listed who entered the Garden of Eden alive.</td></tr>\r\n\r\n<tr class=\"footnotes_plugin_reference_row\"> <th scope=\"row\" id=\"footnote_plugin_reference__1_16\" class=\"footnote_plugin_index pointer\" onclick=\"footnote_moveToAnchor__1('footnote_plugin_tooltip__1_16');\"><a role=\"button\" tabindex=\"0\" class=\"footnote_plugin_link\" >16</a></th> <td class=\"footnote_plugin_text\">Pesikta d-Rav Kahana 11:13</td></tr>\r\n\r\n </tbody> </table> </div></div><script type=\"text/javascript\"> function footnote_expand_reference_container__1() { jQuery('#footnote_references_container__1').show(); jQuery('#footnote_reference_container_collapse_button__1').text('−'); } function footnote_collapse_reference_container__1() { jQuery('#foot